---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE, WHATSAPP } from "../../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout title="Activewear Pricing Strategy and Profit Margins" description="How to price your activewear for maximum profit. Learn cost-plus pricing, competitor analysis, and margin optimization for Amazon, Shopify, and boutique channels.">
    <section style="background:var(--color-primary);color:white;">
    <div style="max-width:56rem;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 1.5rem;text-align:center;">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <span style="font-size:1.5rem;">💰</span>
        <span style="font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-accent-light);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);padding:0.2rem 0.75rem;border-radius:9999px;">Intermediate</span>
        <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#94a3b8;">10 min read</span>
    </div>
    <h1 style="font-size:2.25rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:1rem;">Activewear Pricing Strategy and Profit Margins</h1>
    <p style="color:#94a3b8;max-width:42rem;margin:0 auto;">How to price your activewear for maximum profit. Learn cost-plus pricing, competitor analysis, and margin optimization for Amazon, Shopify, and boutique channels.</p>
    </div>
    </section>

    <div style="max-width:56rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1.5rem;">
    <div style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:1rem;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
    
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Understanding Your Cost Structure</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Before setting prices, know exactly what each unit costs you. Include: product cost, shipping to your warehouse, packaging materials, labeling (FNSKU for Amazon), and estimated customs duties. For a $12 wholesale leggings, your landed cost might be $14-16 per unit when you factor in all expenses.</p>
    


      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Pricing for Amazon FBA</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Amazon fees eat into your margin significantly. Use the FBA calculator: take your selling price, subtract referral fees (8-12% for apparel), subtract FBA fulfillment fees ($3.22-6.50 per unit), subtract your landed cost. Target a minimum of $10-15 net margin per unit for Amazon to be worth your time.</p>
    


      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Shopify and DTC Pricing</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Direct-to-consumer on Shopify allows higher margins (45-65% net after ads) because you control the full price. Price 20-30% above your Amazon price since customers on Shopify are typically more brand-conscious and less price-sensitive.</p>
    


      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Boutique and Retail Pricing</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Boutique buyers expect 50-60% wholesale margin (you sell at 2-2.5x your wholesale price to them). Set wholesale price at 40-50% of MSRP. If retail is $65, your wholesale price should be $26-32 per unit.</p>
    
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-bottom:1.25rem;text-align:center;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-wrap" style="<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
    
      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">What is a healthy profit margin for activewear resale?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Target minimum 40% gross margin on all channels. Amazon FBA typically yields 25-35% net margin after all fees. Shopify DTC can yield 45-65% net margin. Boutiques yield 50-60% margin for the retailer (you get 40-50% of retail as wholesale price).</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">How do I calculate landed cost from China?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Landed cost = product price + shipping (air or sea freight divided by units) + customs duties (typically 10-12% for apparel to US) + port handling fees + last-mile delivery to your warehouse. Use a freight forwarder for the most accurate quotes. For 100 units via air, budget $2-4 per unit additional shipping.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">Should I offer discounts or maintain premium pricing?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">For activewear, avoid discounting on Amazon (it hurts your ranking). On Shopify, use strategic discounts sparingly (Black Friday, New Year). Better strategy: bundle products (2 leggings + 1 sports bra at a slight discount) to increase AOV without devaluing individual items.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">How do I adjust pricing for different markets?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Price by purchasing power parity: US market supports highest prices, UK 10-15% lower, EU similar to US, Australia 5-10% lower, Southeast Asia 30-40% lower. Always quote in USD and let local distributors handle currency conversion. Factor in higher shipping costs to remote regions.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">When should I raise or lower my prices?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Raise prices when: you have strong reviews (4.5+ stars), you are the only seller on a winning product, demand exceeds supply. Lower prices temporarily to win the Buy Box on Amazon or to clear slow-moving inventory. Never race to the bottom on price - focus on value instead.</div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div style="background:var(--color-secondary);border-radius:1.5rem;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Have More Questions?</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Get personalized answers for your specific business on WhatsApp.</p>
      <a href={WHATSAPP} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;background:var(--color-whatsapp);color:white;padding:0.875rem 2rem;border-radius:9999px;font-weight:700;">Ask on WhatsApp</a>
    </div>
    </div>

    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
        {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is a healthy profit margin for activewear resale?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Target minimum 40% gross margin on all channels. Amazon FBA typically yields 25-35% net margin after all fees. Shopify DTC can yield 45-65% net margin. Boutiques yield 50-60% margin for the retailer (you get 40-50% of retail as wholesale price)."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I calculate landed cost from China?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Landed cost = product price + shipping (air or sea freight divided by units) + customs duties (typically 10-12% for apparel to US) + port handling fees + last-mile delivery to your warehouse. Use a freight forwarder for the most accurate quotes. For 100 units via air, budget $2-4 per unit additional shipping."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Should I offer discounts or maintain premium pricing?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For activewear, avoid discounting on Amazon (it hurts your ranking). On Shopify, use strategic discounts sparingly (Black Friday, New Year). Better strategy: bundle products (2 leggings + 1 sports bra at a slight discount) to increase AOV without devaluing individual items."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I adjust pricing for different markets?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Price by purchasing power parity: US market supports highest prices, UK 10-15% lower, EU similar to US, Australia 5-10% lower, Southeast Asia 30-40% lower. Always quote in USD and let local distributors handle currency conversion. Factor in higher shipping costs to remote regions."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "When should I raise or lower my prices?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Raise prices when: you have strong reviews (4.5+ stars), you are the only seller on a winning product, demand exceeds supply. Lower prices temporarily to win the Buy Box on Amazon or to clear slow-moving inventory. Never race to the bottom on price - focus on value instead."
        }
    }
    ],
    })} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": SITE.url },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Resources", "item": SITE.url + "/resources" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Activewear Pricing Strategy and Profit Margins", "item": SITE.url + "/resources/undefined" },
    ],
    })} />

 <!-- FAQ accordion arrow rotation -->
 <script>
 document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach(item => {
   const arrow = item.querySelector('.faq-arrow');
   if (arrow) {
     item.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
       arrow.style.transform = item.open ? 'rotate(180deg)' : 'rotate(0deg)';
     });
   }
 });
 </script>
</BaseLayout>